# server — Progress (Split 13 rewrite)

Tracks progress converting this package from Check! to Split 13. Tags reflect how much Split-13-specific work each file needs, not whether the current Check! code works.

Legend: [COMPLETE] done for Split 13 (either ported, rewritten, or needed no change) · [IN PROGRESS] being worked on now · [NEEDS WORK] exists, must change/be replaced/repurposed · [MISSING] doesn't exist yet, needs to be created · [WARNING] works but flagged for review · [ERROR] known bug

Updated: 2026-08-31 (session 3). Update this file in the same pass as any change to a listed file.

## Top-level config

- .env.example — [COMPLETE] — rewritten for the vars the code actually reads (`PORT`, `CORS_ORIGIN`, `TURN_TIMER_MS`, `BOT_THINK_MIN_MS`/`BOT_THINK_MAX_MS`, `SOCKET_PING_INTERVAL_MS`, `SOCKET_PING_TIMEOUT_MS`); Check!'s MAX_PLAYERS/CARDS_PER_PLAYER/MAX_HAND_SIZE/PEEK_DURATION_MS/MATCHING_STAGE_DURATION_MS/RECONNECT_TIMEOUT_MS/LOBBY_DISCONNECT_TIMEOUT_MS are gone — none of them were read by any file under src/ anymore.
- package.json — [COMPLETE] — described for Split 13.
- tsconfig.json — [COMPLETE]

## src/

- index.ts — [COMPLETE] — socket layer ported. Room settings now carry `botDifficulty` instead of `maxPlayers`; the full-table check reads `seats`; `ACTIONS_REQUIRING_PAYLOAD` covers the new action set; the INITIAL_PEEK re-emit is gone. Rooms, reconnect tokens, lobby codes, session map and the abandoned-game sweep are unchanged and still work.
- game-machine.ts — [COMPLETE] — bot think-time is now randomized per turn (`BOT_THINK_MIN_MS`/`BOT_THINK_MAX_MS`, default 2000-7000ms) as an XState delay *function*, so each bot draws its own beat instead of the table sharing one fixed 1100ms tick — the old pacing made the opening read as machine-gun fire. Written from scratch for Split 13 (~720 lines, replacing Check!'s 95KB engine). Deal 13x4 from a shuffled deck, random starting seat, clockwise turns, throw-one-card, capture on rank match, full table clear, team scoring, 20s turn timer with random auto-throw, bot turns, scoring with draw handling, and Play Again that keeps seats/teams/team wins. `finishHand` is exported so the tie branch can be tested directly.
- state-redactor.ts — [COMPLETE] — rewritten and much smaller. Split 13 hides exactly one thing: an opponent's hand CONTENTS. Own hand is sent in full (sorted), opponents' hands become `null` with `handCount` surviving, and the stack is public in full since every card in it was thrown face-up.
- types.ts — [COMPLETE] — `ServerPlayer` (seat, team, isBot, 13-card hand) and `GameContext` (seats, stack, team scores/counts, playedRankCounts, botDifficulty, turn deadline, result, teamWins) rewritten for Split 13.
- lib/deck-utils.ts — [COMPLETE] — `createDeck`/`shuffleDeck` kept; added `dealHands` (four 13-card hands, asserts a full deck), `sortHand` (rank first so equal ranks sit together — it is a matching game) and `emptyRankCounts`.
- lib/bots.ts — [COMPLETE] — new. Three tiers per rules §11: EASY throws at random, NORMAL captures when it can then dumps its lowest-value card, HARD also captures then prefers throwing a card no opponent can still match (dumping its most expensive card when that is safe). Verified to behave differently: over the same seeds EASY produced 4 captures / 14 stranded where HARD produced 16 / 0.
- lib/logger.ts — [COMPLETE]
- lib/rng.ts — [COMPLETE] — seeded RNG reused as-is; the rules check drives reproducible hands through it.

## Verified

`npm run verify:server` — shared-types and server both typecheck and build clean, and `npm run check:rules` passes: 35 full hands (all three bot tiers, plus a hand where the human never acts and the turn timer carries every one of their turns), the redaction boundary, and the scoring/tie branch.

## Planned / not yet created (Split 13-specific)

- Nothing outstanding on the server for a playable v1. Open items are per-seat bot difficulty (see design-vault/Redesign/Open Questions.md) and porting `.env.example`.
